course: dictionary
lesson: 15033
title: Resultant: what follows, and the single force
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Resultant» comes from the word result, which means what happens because of something else. When an adjective describes a thing, it tells you more about it. «The storm broke the windows, and the resultant floods closed the town.» The floods came because of the storm, so resultant means happening as a result of the storm.
explain: In science, resultant has a special meaning. «Two forces pushed the box: 10 N to the right and 4 N to the left.» Opposite forces cancel, so take the smaller from the bigger: 10 minus 4 is 6. The resultant force is 6 N to the right, one single force with the same effect as both together.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a simple word. «The resultant damage was huge» can become «the damage that resulted was huge». If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Resultant means happening as a result of something.
fact: Resultant can be an adjective, as in «the resultant damage», or a noun, as in «a resultant».
fact: In science, the resultant force is the single force that has the same effect as several forces together.
fact: To find a resultant force, subtract forces that push in opposite directions, and add forces that push in the same direction.
fact: «Resultant changes» means changes that came from something that happened before.
exercise: «The storm broke the windows, and the resultant floods closed the town.» What does resultant mean here? | Sudden and noisy | Very large and wide | *Happening as a result of the storm | Made of water only
exercise: «A push of 10 N to the right and 4 N to the left gives a resultant force.» What is the resultant force? | *6 N to the right | 6 N to the left | 14 N to the right | 4 N to the right
exercise: In «the resultant damage was huge», which word could replace resultant without changing the meaning? | *resulting | empty | happy | quiet
test: Two forces act on a car: 8 N forward and 3 N backward. What is the resultant force? | *5 N forward | 8 N backward | 11 N forward | 3 N forward
test: «The resultant changes to the timetable confused the pupils.» What does resultant mean here? | *Changes that happened because of something | Changes to the weather | Changes that are very small | Changes the pupils made on purpose
exam: Two forces of 12 N left and 9 N left act on a box. What is the resultant force? | 21 N right | 3 N right | *21 N left | 3 N left
